# ENGINE_2 -- Novelty

Use when the user asks "is this too close to X" or after ENGINE_1 before
heavy implementation.

```bash
python3 scripts/check_novelty.py --slug <slug>
```

A high local score means change the **problem**, not the wording. The local
check only sees this machine's `drafts/`. Also ask: would a frontier model
treat this as a named exercise?

Difficulty angle: a reskin of a saturated bug lattice (checksum + staging +
export, LRU, parser-from-spec-only) is both a novelty fail and a difficulty
fail. Do not "unique-ify" by swapping domain nouns onto the same traps.

## Required reply

```text
Engine: 2
Nearest local draft: <slug> score=<n>
Conceptual overlap: <what is the same engineering problem>
Change if too close: <new trap / new interface / new family-native work>
```
